    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i tried a version of this yesterday and it was intense. i had this huge spike, like 98% certainty, that a specific trader on a forum was going to liquidate a massive position in a penny stock. i didn't even know who he was, i just felt the math hit. ten minutes later, the volume exploded exactly like i \"saw.\" \n\nit's starting to feel like these aren't just random thoughts, but like i'm tapping into a latent variable in the market's probability field. how can we differentiate between standard pattern recognition and these higher-order probability spikes in our modeling? i don't want to confuse the two.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
